hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20621","Bahz and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, they said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Murrah al-Bahzi, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Bahz said in his hadith, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An upheaval will rage like horns, and this one and those with him are upon the truth. He said: So I went and took hold of the edge of his garment, and there he was Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him."
"20622","He narrated to us [Source text truncated in index: Haddathana only]."
"20643","Abu Usamah Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, Kahmas informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, Harami ibn al-Harith and Usamah ibn Khuraym narrated to me, and they used to raid together, and they narrated to me a hadith, neither one of them feeling that his companion had narrated it to me, from Murrah al-Bahzi, he said: While we were with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a road of the roads of Madinah, he said: How will you act in a fitnah that will rage in the regions of the earth as if it were bovine horns? They said: What shall we do, O Prophet of Allah? He said: Adhere to this and his companions, or: Follow this and his companions. He said: So I hastened until I was exhausted, then I caught up with the man and said: This, O Messenger of Allah? He said: This, and there he was Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: This and his companions, and he mentioned him."
